  "notes": [
    "CRACKLE measure centroid is the only per-cell radial coordinate in the vocabulary guaranteed concentric with the tessellation, which is exactly what this needed: SPOTS and DAPPLES lay down their own centres from their own seed, and those have never had anything to do with where a wall fell.",
    "A ring is an outer centroid mask times an inner one inverted. If the rings come out as filled discs instead, the field runs the other way and the two inverts want swapping. Paint the four layers in flat primaries and look before changing anything else - reasoning about this costs an evening and looking costs one bake.",
    "scale is 9 rather than the default 5 on purpose. At 5 a cell radius is about 2.5 units and 0.20 of that is under one texel, so the central pip would be arithmetically present and invisible on the horse.",
    "The PATCHES mask is the whole of the restraint. Without it this tiles the entire barrel, which is what the source image actually looked like and is not what this gene is for."
  ]
